# Argued-for cases for scripts/check-nothing-identifying.py.
#
# Format, tab-separated: <path>	<the source line>	<why this one is fine>
#
# Keyed by the source line rather than by line number, so moving code does not
# silently re-allow something and editing the line does not either.
#
# The bar: the API may be used to decide *where Loupe writes on this machine*.
# It may never be used to decide *what goes into a bundle*. A bundle is pasted
# into tickets and public repositories; a path on somebody's disk is not.

Sources/LoupeCore/Transport.swift	return URL(fileURLWithPath: NSHomeDirectory())	Chooses where to write bundles on this machine - ~/.loupe/<app>. The path never enters a bundle, and Catalyst has no homeDirectoryForCurrentUser.
